PowerBI-Projects
📊 Power BI Data Analytics Projects
Welcome to my Power BI Projects directory! This folder contains a collection of data analysis, data modeling, DAX engineering, and data visualization projects executed to build an ATS-optimized, recruiter-ready data analytics portfolio.

📁 Featured Projects
1. Apex Innovation Operational and Financial Reports
Description: A comprehensive retail analytics dashboard designed to monitor and evaluate operational and financial performance.

Key Techniques: Star Schema Data Modeling, Advanced DAX, Troubleshooting.

Objective: To architect a robust data model, resolve complex business logic errors, filter out "blank" values, and fix double-counting anomalies in revenue metrics through precise line-item calculations.

2. Adventure_Works_Financial_Reports
Description: A financial reporting suite built using the industry-standard Adventure Works enterprise dataset.

Key Techniques: DAX Formulation, Time Intelligence, Enterprise Configuration.

Objective: To calculate profitability, profit margins, and organizational costs over various periods, demonstrating readiness for complex, real-world corporate data environments.

3. Financial_Dashboard_Chocolate_Ltd.
Description: A combined sales and financial performance dashboard tailored for corporate tracking within the retail and FMCG sectors.

Key Techniques: Power Query ETL, Data Integration, Visual Storytelling.

Objective: To build robust pipelines to clean, shape, and integrate raw sales datasets, and to track product performance, regional distribution, and revenue trends.

4. Quarterly_Financial_Reports_of_XYZ_Ltd.
Description: A structured reporting tool focused on automating routine, quarter-over-quarter financial analytics.

🛠️ Skills & Tools Demonstrated
Core BI Tools: Power BI, DAX, Power Query.

Data Technologies: SQL, Microsoft Excel.

Data Architecture: Enterprise-level data architecture, Star Schemas (Dimensional Modeling), ETL processes, and professional-grade visualization.

Domain Knowledge: Direct application of business and commerce studies (corporate finance, cost accounting, and economics) into analytical workflows.

